      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T14:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fallback fires whenever _boot_seq is empty, but _boot_seq \u003d\u003d \u0027BootSeq\u0027 also when BootMode was successfully read as \u0027Bios\u0027 (get_bios_boot_mode returns \u0027Bios\u0027 on KeyError and get_boot_seq returns \u0027BootSeq\u0027 for any non-Uefi BootMode). On a Legacy host with empty BootSeq and a stale populated UefiBootSeq, boot_seq_attr becomes \u0027UefiBootSeq\u0027 and patch_boot_seq PATCHes UefiBootSeq, which does not govern legacy boot order: silent no-op or 400. The comment above assumes empty BootSeq implies unreadable BootMode. Consider gating the fallback on the BootMode read actually failing (get_boot_seq conveying \u0027unknown\u0027), and test that alongside this test\u0027s case.",
      "revId": "bb98eb218c5b36daa19a152e50d6ae7985ac37c4",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
