      "side": 1,
      "message": "Behavior regression vs parent: parent\u0027s get_job_queue returned [] for any non-200 from {manager}/Jobs (the regex simply matched nothing), so clear_job_queue/change_boot proceeded. Now find_jobs_resource() raises BadfishException when neither candidate returns 200 and get_job_queue propagates it. Verified A/B: mocked 404 -\u003e parent returns [], patchset raises. Affects hosts with an inaccessible Jobs collection (401/403 restricted roles, special firmware) and list_job_queue; in the quads move flow change_boot is Dell-gated (release/standard.py prepare_host_hardware), so healthy iDRAC9/10 are unaffected. Suggest catching BadfishException here and returning [] (parent semantics), or making the resolver return a \u0027not supported\u0027 signal and deciding per caller. Also no test covers the rerouted callers (get_job_queue/get_job_status/delete_job_queue_force/clear_job_list/create_bios_config_job), which is why this slipped; add one with an OEM_JOBS mock.",
      "revId": "bb98eb218c5b36daa19a152e50d6ae7985ac37c4",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
